  "headline": "FDA's shortage list shows methylprednisolone acetate injection current since 2021-12-15 with multiple manufacturers listed; the 20 mg/mL 5 mL vial used at Corvale sites is labeled by Pharmacia & Upjohn Company LLC (FEI 1810189) whose most recent inspection ended 2023-06-16 classified VAI, 548 days after the initial posting",
  "headline_cites": ["E27", "E22", "E23", "E24", "E25", "E26", "E18", "D10"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "FDA's shortage list for methylprednisolone acetate injection shows the shortage as Current with an initial posting date of 2021-12-15 and lists Amneal Pharmaceuticals, Eugia US LLC, Par Health USA LLC, Pfizer Inc., and Sagent Pharmaceuticals as affected companies.",
      "cites": ["E27", "E22", "E23", "E24", "E25", "E26"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The 20 mg/mL 5 mL vial used at Corvale East and Corvale General carries NDC 00009027401 and is labeled by Pharmacia & Upjohn Company LLC (FEI 1810189).",
      "cites": ["E1", "E6", "E18"]
    },
    {
      "text": "FDA inspection 1208260 at that plant ended 2023-06-16 and was classified VAI, with the classification letter dated 2024-09-10, which was 548 days after the shortage was first posted on 2021-12-15.",
      "cites": ["D10", "E17"]
    },
    {
      "text": "No FDA inspection at the registered plant is recorded as OAI, and no FDA action at that plant is documented before the 2021-12-15 posting.",
      "cites": ["E10", "E11", "E12", "E13", "E14", "E15", "E16", "E17"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Corvale East has 2.7 days of the 20 mg/mL 5 mL vial on hand while Corvale General has 22.8 days, and the rule‑ranked transfer option moves 61 vials from Corvale General to Corvale East, leaving the sender with 14 days and the receiver with 13 days.",
      "cites": ["D1", "D2", "D12"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The transfer requires a pharmacy director transfer request and is the highest‑ranked mitigation under the current allocation rules.",
      "cites": ["D12"]
    }
  ]
}
